# Eigenbases. The paper is reproduced from the float64 .npz bases, so every mesh
# ships its .npz. The nine paper meshes ALSO ship a .json: that is the float32 asset
# the web application renders, and it is NOT a faithful reproduction source (float32
# rounding shifts the epsilon-threshold nodal crossings and moves beta_0 by a few
# percent). The analysis loaders prefer .npz for this reason; a .json fallback exists
# only as a last resort and warns that it is approximate. Nothing here is ignored;
# the double_torus 4846-vertex ablation basis in particular has no regenerable source
# (its .obj is a different 19562-vertex remesh) and exists only as this committed file.

# Experiment eigen (genus sequence, symmetry-breaking octahedra): .npz is committed,
# the .json duplicate is not. Regenerate either with experiment.precompute_experiment_eigen.
data/experiments/eigen/*.json

# Superseded eigenbases kept only as local history.
*.bak
*.bak2

# Web data copied in Step 5 (from data/eigen, can ignore)
webapp/public/data/

# Downloaded meshes (Stanford etc., optional commit)
data/meshes/*.obj

# Step 4 / paper output. These CSVs are what the paper's "Supplementary material"
# and "Data availability" sections point readers to, so they are committed. Only the
# bulky eigen intermediates under remeshed_genus/ are ignored; the convergence CSVs
# derived from them are kept, and run_remeshed_genus_pipeline.py rebuilds the rest.
data/results/remeshed_genus/eigen/
# Legacy: scripts used to write to a results/ dir at the repo root; now unified to
# data/results/. Anchored with a leading slash: unanchored "results/" matches at any
# depth and would silently swallow data/results/ as well.
/results/

# Webapp
webapp/node_modules/
webapp/dist/

